Use the IN operator for the array value in the registrations view query alter.

recurring_events_views_views_query_alter() adds a raw Views where condition
whose value is a one-element array but whose operator is "=". Drupal 11 throws
an InvalidQueryException ("Calling Condition::condition() without an array
compatible operator is not supported"), so /events/{eventinstance}/registrations
returns a 500. Use "IN" so the array value is valid.

Report upstream and drop this patch once fixed there.

--- a/modules/recurring_events_views/recurring_events_views.module
+++ b/modules/recurring_events_views/recurring_events_views.module
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@
           $query->where[1]['conditions'][] = [
             'field' => $field,
             'value' => $value,
-            'operator' => '=',
+            'operator' => 'IN',
           ];
         }
       }
